  "query_preview": "..FOR EXTREME SOUTHWESTERN CALIFORNIA INCLUDING ORANGE...\nSAN DIEGO...WESTERN RIVERSIDE AND SOUTHWESTERN SAN BERNARDINO\nCOUNTIES...\n\nThis afternoon...the thick band of mid and high clouds that\nbrought us rain and showers overnight has moved east and south as\nthe low pressure system to our northwest moves to the southeast.\nThis low pressure system has brought us cooler conditions and\nstronger onshore flow. Temperatures are mostly lower than at this\ntime yesterday, especially in the mountains and deserts where\ntemperatures are anywhere from 3-12 degrees lower. High \ntemperatures will be a few degrees lower today, followed by \nwarming on Tuesday and greater inland warming on Wednesday. High \ntemperatures on Wednesday will range from around 80 near the coast\nto the upper 80s to mid 90s for the Inland Empire with the lower \ndeserts in the upper 90s. The onshore flow is currently producing\nwesterly winds gusting 25-30 mph in the mountain passes, canyons\nand on adjacent desert slopes. The gusty westerly winds will\nweaken this evening. Low clouds persist over and west of the\nmountains. Significant moisture remains through a depth of the \natmosphere and the possibility of showers over the mtns can't be\neliminated, but conditions are stable enough to make that outcome\nunlikely.\n\nBy Tuesday morning, the low pressure system will move far enough\nto the southeast so that the upper low is over the lower Colorado\nRiver valley with northerly winds aloft on the west side of the\nupper low. A warming trend begins on Tuesday with locally gusty north\nto northeast winds at the surface.\n\nThursday into early next week... High pressure aloft will \ncontinue the warming trend into the weekend with only slight \ncooling on Sunday. Widespread moderate or greater HeatRisk is \nexpected for the coast and valleys for Thursday through the\nweekend, with widespread major HeatRisk for inland coastal areas \nand the western San Diego County valleys. \n\nHigh temperatures for next weekend will range from a few degrees \nabove average for the lower deserts to as much as 12 to 18 degrees\nabove average for the coast and valleys in San Diego County. High\ntemperatures for next weekend will range from the 80s near the \ncoast to the mid 90s to around 100 for the inland valleys with the\nlower deserts around 100. \n\nFor the weekend, overnight low temperatures for the Orange County\ncoastal plain, and for the coast and western valleys in San Diego\nCounty will be mostly in the lower to mid 70s. For Friday through\nSunday, there could be several records tied or broken for record \nwarm low temperatures, mostly for coastal and valley locations. \nThe existing records for some of those locations was from 1997.",
